{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792887671,"nonce":"xcR30c0ds11jvudHF/gNv7Stkp8=","title":"The heap keeps its peak footprint after the live set falls","message":"Caribou's heap is Ash's Immix collector as of late September. Ash has since\ntaught it to give memory back; caribou's copy has none of that, so a program's\nfootprint stays at its peak for the rest of the run.\n\nReproducer (headless Haxe): fill a static with 3000 arrays of 10000 floats,\nnull the static, and call `hl.Gc.major()` twice at each stage, sleeping 6 s\nbetween stages and 40 s before the last.\n\n| stage   | live    | ash footprint | caribou footprint |\n|---------|---------|---------------|-------------------|\n| start   |         | 9.6 MB        | 15 MB             |\n| burst   | 283 MB  | 353 MB        | 685 MB            |\n| dropped | 0.1 MB  | 72 MB         | 685 MB            |\n| quiet   | 0.1 MB  | 72 MB         | 685 MB            |\n\nCaribou's 685 MB is 610 MB of untagged VM_ALLOCATE (the heap reservation's\nresident free blocks) and 58 MB of MALLOC_LARGE.\n\nWhy:\n- A collection hands back only the blocks it freed itself, and only when the\n  previous collection was a heartbeat (30 s) ago. The first of two back-to-back\n  majors frees the blocks but is not quiet; a later quiet one frees nothing new,\n  so nothing goes back.\n- There is no idle collection, so a program that stops allocating never\n  collects again.\n- The trigger grows to 512 MB, so the peak is about twice Ash's.\n\nAsh commits to port:\n- b57fae83: collect and hand pages back when every mutator has been idle\n- 781ebbba: return deferred free pages (`pending_handback`) on a quiet or idle\n  collection\n- 3cd93519: hand malloc's free pages back when the world goes idle\n- 3bd86d4e, 64c6850d: hand back in chunks; an idle collection hands back all\n- ab1eddd5, b0a5df76, ebbd5e3b: pacing, allocation between collections held to\n  about two live sets, a major once the live set is 1.5x the last major's, and\n  an explicit collection does not widen the trigger\n\nReported by the ChimpMonk session: the editor at 921 MB footprint with a 71 MB\nlive Haxe heap, against Ash's 595 MB and then 278 MB.","files":null}]}